.TH AVR\-LOG\-SEARCH 1 "" "avr 0.1.4" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-log-search \- Search logs for a repository.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr log search
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search logs for a repository.
.PP
Performs full-text search when --query is provided, otherwise returns logs sorted by line number. Results are filtered to logs from repositories you have access to.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr log search --repo acme/web --query "error"
    avr log search --repo rep-abc123 --level error --limit 50
    avr log search --repo rep-abc123 --vm-id vm-xyz --stream stderr
    avr log search --repo rep-abc123 --query "OOM" --json content,timestamp,vm_id
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    content, group_name, id, level, line_number, repository_id, score,
    step_name, step_record_id, stream, timestamp, vm_id
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-query\fR \fITEXT\fR
Full-text search query
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by output stream (choices: stdout, stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by log level (choices: debug, info, warning, error)
.TP
\fB\-\-vm\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by execution/VM ID
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Maximum results to return (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-log (1)
